@startuml

title Lab4 - DAO Pattern (Score Board)
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0

package dao {
  enum GameDifficulty {
    EASY
    NORMAL
    HARD
  }

  class ScoreRecord <<Value Object>> {
    - playerName:String
    - score:int
    - recordTime:LocalDateTime
    + getPlayerName():String
    + getScore():int
    + getRecordTime():LocalDateTime
    + formatRecordTime():String
    + toTsvLine():String
  }

  interface ScoreRecordDao <<DAO Pattern>> {
    + getAllRecords():List<ScoreRecord>
    + addRecord(ScoreRecord scoreRecord):void
    + deleteRecord(ScoreRecord scoreRecord):boolean
  }

  class FileScoreRecordDao <<DAO Impl>> {
    - filePath:Path
    + getAllRecords():List<ScoreRecord>
    + addRecord(ScoreRecord scoreRecord):void
    + deleteRecord(ScoreRecord scoreRecord):boolean
    + getFilePath():Path
  }

  class ScoreBoardService {
    - difficulty:GameDifficulty
    - scoreRecordDao:ScoreRecordDao
    + recordScore(String playerName, int score):void
    + getSortedRecords():List<ScoreRecord>
    + deleteRecordByRank(int rank):boolean
    + printScoreBoard():void
  }
}

package application {
  class Game {
    - difficulty:GameDifficulty
    - scoreBoardService:ScoreBoardService
    + Game()
    + Game(GameDifficulty difficulty)
    + action():void
  }
}

ScoreRecordDao <|.. FileScoreRecordDao
ScoreBoardService --> ScoreRecordDao : access data
ScoreBoardService --> ScoreRecord : sort / rank
FileScoreRecordDao --> ScoreRecord : read / write
FileScoreRecordDao --> GameDifficulty : resolve file
Game --> ScoreBoardService : record and print
Game --> GameDifficulty : current difficulty

note right of ScoreRecordDao
<<DAO Pattern>>
Data access logic is separated from
score sorting and console presentation.
end note

@enduml
